// NOTE: intentionally no COURSES/CUISINES export here anymore. CATALOG is a
// fixed 99-recipe snapshot (SL-Cook100 only), so deriving filter option
// lists from it meant any recipe imported later -- e.g. the 13,463-row
// "International" batch -- could add real rows to the DB whose
// `course`/`cuisine` values could never appear as a selectable filter
// (every one of those rows shares the single literal cuisine value
// "International", and all of them have `course = NULL`, so a `course`
// chip built this way could only ever match Sri Lankan rows). Course and
// cuisine filter options now come from the live `GET /api/recipes/facets`
// endpoint (see recipesApi.facets in lib/api.ts) so newly imported values
// show up automatically with no regeneration step. CATALOG itself is still
// used as a static id->metadata lookup elsewhere (e.g. UseItUpPage,
// RecipeDetailPage) and is unaffected by this change.